    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 201202\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n402 AM PST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* A few weak disturbances will roll through the area over the next\n  few days, bringing light snow showers to the Sierra. Otherwise,\n  weather across the rest of the region will remain relatively\n  benign with temperatures warming up next week.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Thanksgiving.\n\nShowers have cleared out of the area as we find ourselves behind the \naxis of the trough responsible for Thursday's unsettled weather. A \nsecondary vorticity lobe will swing through southeastern California, \nsouthern Nevada, and northwestern Arizona today, bringing a 20 to \n40% chance of light showers to the higher terrain of Inyo County and \nsouthern Nevada this afternoon and evening. A transient shortwave \nridge will set up over the area on Saturday, providing a reprieve \nfrom the active weather of the past few days. A shortwave trough \nwill move through late Sunday into Monday, bringing a breezy \nwesterly winds and few inches of new snow to the Sierra Crest. \nOtherwise, the only evidence of this system passing through will be \nincreased cloud cover. Ridging will set up over the Western US on \nTuesday and Wednesday, allowing for temperatures to warm back up to \nmore seasonable temperatures for late November. The forecast becomes \nmore uncertain late in the week as guidance continues to highlight \nthe potential for another trough to impact the Western US, with \ninterensemble discrepancies regarding the evolution of this system. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...\nGusty south winds overnight have finally diminished to 8 kt or less \nand should remain light through the morning hours becoming variable \nat times. Wind will favor a NNE direction during the afternoon but \nshould remain below 8 kt. A period a stronger NW winds around 10 kt \nis possible tomorrow night from 03z-09z. Guidance shows these winds \ndiminishing and becoming southerly after 09z but confidence on exact \ntiming of that is lower. Mainly clear skies this morning then expect \nafternoon and evening cumulus clouds around 08-10 kft. Any shower \nactivity tomorrow should remain in the higher terrain and not impact \nthe terminal. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Much quieter conditions \nexpected through the TAF period. The only exception will be KDAG \nwhere strong west winds 15-20 kt with gusts to 30 kt persist into \nthis evening, then slowly diminish later tonight. There is potential \nfor a period of stronger NW winds 10-15 kt in the Las Vegas Valley \nafter 03z tonight. Elsewhere, expect fairly light winds favoring \nnortherly directions. Ceilings remain VFR through the period. \n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Stessman\nAVIATION...Moore\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
